1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,310
This scrap was hidden in a tiny pocket inside a dead man's

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:03,970
trousers.

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:04,780
Two words.

4
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:05,530
Tamam Shud.

5
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:06,770
Persian for, ended.

6
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,770
Somerton Beach, Adelaide.

7
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:11,150
The first of December, 1948.

8
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:13,600
A well-dressed man, dead against the seawall.

9
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:14,420
No ID.

10
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:16,880
The labels on his clothes had been cut out.

11
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,840
Weeks later, a suitcase linked to him turned up at Adelaide railway

12
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:21,360
station.

13
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,070
Its label?

14
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:23,030
Removed too.

15
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:26,780
Then someone handed police the very book that scrap was torn from.

16
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,970
The Rubaiyat of Omar Khayyam.

17
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,730
On the back cover, in pencil:

18
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:32,740
a phone number, and lines of letters.

19
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:33,370
A code.

20
00:00:33,390 --> 00:00:34,880
Nobody has ever cracked it.

21
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:35,900
Cause of death?

22
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:36,920
Never determined.

23
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:38,150
Poison was suspected.

24
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,130
None was found.

25
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:39,700
Spy.

26
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:40,280
Lost love.

27
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:40,790
Suicide.

28
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:42,600
Plenty of theories, no proof.

29
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:46,400
Then, in 2021, police exhumed his body.

30
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:51,070
In 2022, a professor and a genealogist tested hairs from his plaster

31
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:51,770
death mask.

32
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,520
The DNA led through family trees to a name.

33
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:56,140
Carl, Charles, Webb.

34
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:59,660
An electrical engineer from Melbourne, born 1905.

35
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:01,090
But it isn't official.

36
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:03,520
Police and the coroner haven't confirmed it yet.

37
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,480
And even if he is Webb, no one knows how he died.

38
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:07,880
Or what the code says.

39
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:10,190
So what do you think those letters spell?

40
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:12,090
It all comes back to this.
